This extension adds Crimson Desert modding support to Vortex Mod Manager.
[summary]DMM installed automatically.[/summary]

[b]✅ Supported Versions:[/b]
[list]
[*]Steam[/*]
[*]Epic[/*]
[*]Xbox[/*]
[*]Other versions may need to select the installation location manually.[/*]
[/list]
[b]🛠️ Mod Installation Notes:[/b]
[list]
[*]Root Folder mods with a "bin64" folder install to the game folder.[/*]
[*]Definitive Mod Manager installs to the game folder, recognised by a ".exe" file.[/*]
[*]Tools mods with a "CD JSON Mod Manager.exe", "CrimsonSharp.exe", "CrimsonSaveEditorStandalone.exe", "PazGui.exe", "CDModManager.exe", "QT_ModManager.exe" or "CrimsonDesertModManager.exe" file install to the game folder.[/*]
[*]Special Patch mods with a ".dll", ".asi" or ".addon64" file install to the game folder.[/*]
[*]Crimson Sharp mods with a "manifest.json" file, a "files" folder and a "meta" or "0000" to "0035" folder install to the "mods" folder.[/*]
[*]Patch mods with a "modinfo.json" file install to the "mods" folder.[/*]
[*]Texture mods are recognised by a "meta" or "0000" to "0035" folder and a ".dds" file.[/*]
[*]JSON mods with a ".json" file install to the "mods" folder.[/*]
[*]Binaries (Engine Injector) mods with a ".dll", ".asi" or ".addon64" file install to the "bin64" folder.[/*]
[*]Any other mod not described above installs to the game folder.[/*]
[*]Archives with a FOMOD installer (a "fomod" folder with ModuleConfig.xml) are handed to Vortex's built-in FOMOD installer instead.[/*]
[/list]
[b]📋 Usage Notes:[/b]
[list]
[*]You can open several useful files/folders/URLs using the buttons within the folder icon on the Mods toolbar.[/*]
[*]Supports mods for [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/crimsondesert/mods/84?tab=description]Crimson Browser[/url]﻿ ("manifest.json" and "files" folder) and [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/crimsondesert/mods/633]DMM[/url] (.json file or "00XX" folder). Installs mods to the "mods" folder. [b][color=#ffff00]You must run the tool to complete mod install.[/color][/b][/*]
[*]Installs multiple tools, like [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/crimsondesert/mods/62?tab=posts]Unpacker [/url]and [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/crimsondesert/mods/20]Save Editor[/url]﻿ ﻿to game root folder. Includes a launch tool.[/*]
[*]All other mods installed to game root folder with a fallback notification.[/*]
[*][size=2]Includes launch tools for multiple managers and other tools.﻿﻿[/size][/*]
[/list]

[b]📝 Notes for Mod Authors:[/b]
[spoiler]
Packaging rules for Crimson Desert mods, so Vortex installs them to the right place.

Vortex decides what a mod is by looking at the files and folders inside the archive. It tries each installer in order and the first one that matches wins, so archive layout is what determines where your mod ends up.

========================================================================

Root / Game Folder Mods:

For mods laid out the same way the files appear inside the game folder. Vortex copies the matched folder and everything under it straight into the game.

[code]
MyRootMod.zip
└── bin64\
    └── ... files in their real relative locations
[/code]

  Requirements:
    - Recognised by a folder named "bin64" in the archive.

  Installs to: the game folder

  Common mistakes:
    - Zipping the folder that CONTAINS the game folders, instead of the game folders themselves, adds an extra level and misplaces every file.

========================================================================

Dmm:

Recognised when the archive contains a ".exe" file.

  Installs to: the game folder

========================================================================

Tools:

Recognised when the archive contains a "CD JSON Mod Manager.exe", "CrimsonSharp.exe", "CrimsonSaveEditorStandalone.exe", "PazGui.exe", "CDModManager.exe", "QT_ModManager.exe" or "CrimsonDesertModManager.exe" file.

  Installs to: the game folder

========================================================================

Specialpatchmod:

Recognised when the archive contains a ".dll", ".asi" or ".addon64" file.

  Installs to: the game folder

========================================================================

Browsermod:

Recognised when the archive contains a "manifest.json" file, a "files" folder and a "meta", "0000", "0001", "0002", "0003", "0004", "0005", "0006", "0007", "0008", "0009", "0010", "0011", "0012", "0013", "0014", "0015", "0016", "0017", "0018", "0019", "0020", "0021", "0022", "0023", "0024", "0025", "0026", "0027", "0028", "0029", "0030", "0031", "0032", "0033", "0034" or "0035" folder.

  Installs to: "mods"

========================================================================

Patchmod:

Recognised when the archive contains a "modinfo.json" file.

  Installs to: "mods"

========================================================================

Texture:

Recognised when the archive contains a "meta", "0000", "0001", "0002", "0003", "0004", "0005", "0006", "0007", "0008", "0009", "0010", "0011", "0012", "0013", "0014", "0015", "0016", "0017", "0018", "0019", "0020", "0021", "0022", "0023", "0024", "0025", "0026", "0027", "0028", "0029", "0030", "0031", "0032", "0033", "0034" or "0035" folder and a ".dds" file.

========================================================================

Json:

Recognised when the archive contains a ".json" file.

  Installs to: "mods"

========================================================================

Binaries:

Recognised when the archive contains a ".dll", ".asi" or ".addon64" file.

  Installs to: "bin64"

========================================================================

Fallback Installer:

The catch-all. Any archive that matched none of the installers above lands here and is copied across unchanged.

[b][color=#ffff00]NOTE: Landing in the fallback installer is a signal your archive layout needs fixing.[/color][/b]

  Requirements:
    - Reaching this installer usually means the archive was not laid out in a way Vortex recognised.
    - Vortex shows the user a notification when a mod installs through the fallback.

  Installs to: the game folder

  Common mistakes:
    - If your mod lands here unintentionally, re-check the layouts above - users will see a fallback warning and may report the mod as broken.

========================================================================

Rules That Apply To Every Mod Type:

    - Archives containing a FOMOD installer (a "fomod" folder with ModuleConfig.xml) are handed to the built-in FOMOD installer instead.
    - Folder and file name matching is case-insensitive.
    - Extra wrapper folders around a recognised folder are generally fine.
[/spoiler]

